@essay id="p4-intro" rh="THE HOUSE OF VANE · HOW TO USE THIS PART"
# The family and its paper
drop: The Temple teaches that God chose Elias Vane to restore the nation and that his bloodline carries the anointing forward. In the Crownward that isn't a metaphor. It shapes every interaction the family has with everyone else (CR). The House of Vane is the only household in the book where theology is the family business.
The Final Rulings rebuilt this family. Dorian's parent was Elias's elder child and the rightful successor, removed in 2061 when Dorian was a child. Crest, the younger sibling, took the throne by survivorship and knew the shape of what he sat on (FR 35–37, 39). Dorian was spared because a child's claim can be supervised (FR 38). The ledger Azrael found named Elias, and Dorian has known that since 2061 (FR 44).
Everyone in this part performs for the Broadcast, and the dossiers keep asking what each of them does in the rooms it can't film: the Study, the side rooms at the Anointed Evening, the Binding Night, the Sovereign Garden behind its gates (CR).
side:
chips: CR, TL, FR 35–44
k: Ages in 2104
stext: Dorian 59 (Ruling). Lyris 58. Azrael 27. Judah 25. The Prelate 67 (CR, TL).
marg
see: Vol. I, the family tree, {v1:tree}. The Crown, {v1:crown}.
/end

